# Boot to the Corn tutorial and then STOP PRESSING THINGS.  For A/B timing.
#
# new_game.pad keeps its START/START/A group going to t=71 so that a run which
# took the slow path through the logos still gets its presses. That is right
# for reaching gameplay unattended and wrong for measuring, because the title
# arrives around t=47 and every press after that lands in play: START is PAUSE,
# and the A that follows it is navigating a pause menu. Two runs given that
# schedule can end up in two different places, and then their frame counts are
# not comparable -- which is the exact trap the handover warns about under
# "never compare two runs' totals without checking how far each got".
#
# So this is the same groups with the tail cut off at the first arrival. A run
# that is unlucky in the logos will not reach the tutorial at all; that shows
# up as a low flip count and a scene that is not 61, and the run is discarded
# rather than compared.
#
# Measure the window, not the run: the cumulative [FRAME] line includes boot,
# which is I/O bound and identical either way. Take flips between two reports
# once the scene is settled.

12.0:START  13.5:START  15.0:A
20.0:START  21.5:START  23.0:A
28.0:START  29.5:START  31.0:A
36.0:START  37.5:START  39.0:A
44.0:START  45.5:START  47.0:A
